The source distribution vendors PipeCraft 1.5.0-alpha.1 so the Styler installer
can build a private Rust binary when Cargo is available. PipeCraft owns DAG
scheduling, global resource coordination, process supervision, cancellation,
events and durable job/resume state. Styler owns Linux/domain semantics,
receipts, backups, reconciliation, Apply/Undo meaning and the user interface.

A local Python runtime remains temporarily as a compatibility backend for tests,
extensions that require in-process Python objects, and installations where the
Rust binary is not yet available. It is not the target production architecture.
